"Every Spire holds a chained augera, bound in a crystal dodecahedron in its top chamber."
"The dodecahedron is cloudy, milky-white crystal edged in metal shifting black, silver and gold."
"The dodecahedron floats and spins over a floor glyph circle with a bare, mirror-black centre."
"Golden floor glyphs, in no public set, hum like an orchestra, holding the crystal aloft and shut."
"The Academy Spire's top chamber is 5 storeys high, spans the Spire, and has a glass pyramid apex."
"A private elevator with Advanced Set barrier glyphs rises to diamond-handled chamber doors."
"The diamond-handled doors open by touch and focus, only for those the Spire permits."
"A Spire's threshold sweeps arcanic pressure over those who enter, scrutinising and judging them."
"Those who enter the Geldor Spire are carried straight to the augera's chamber."
"The augera call the crystal a knot-link-anchor, and a chained augera a woven-shackled-stream."
"The knot-link-anchor ties an augera to its place and gives it a new aspect."
"The anchor also calms an agitated augera and gives visitors a point of reference."
"An augera is a primal force of arcana; augera is an ancient mortal name for such a being."
"The augera call their raw state raw-boundless-tempest."
"Augera are echoes of the wellspring-ocean-core, a vastly greater being deep in oblivion."
"The wellspring turned away from the augera; they revere it and fear to speak its name."
"A wellspring has no emotional bleed or alien feel: a completely clean presence."
"Near a wellspring, space and time warp; phantom mountains not found in the Empire can appear."
"Augera speak in hyphenated bundles of concepts; grasping them can overwhelm or knock one out."
"Some augera concepts cannot be understood by mortals; trying brings vertigo and vomiting."
"Augera words include flavour-vein-echo, a signature, and touch-speak-bend, to ensorcel."
"Augera name people by aspects of their flares, such as warm-skilful-bridge or cold-strong-watcher."
"Augera call Demiurge Caldwell white-bright-power."
"Augera retain every detail of each person they touch; \"We are the web; the web remembers.\""
"Augera adapt to the frame of whoever sees them; the lake augera wore Jerric's dead mother's face."
"To others the lake augera appeared as a void of inky tendrils, drawn from their fears."
"Wild augera, echoes of echoes, remain unchained in wild places."
"Wild augera have a gentle aspect, drifting-pool-channel, safe for mortals to address."
"Wild augera have a raw aspect, raw-boundless-tempest, of primordial power, dangerous to engage."
"Pre-arcanophany sages tried and failed to tame the wild augera."
"Atrael Ka'atus, a very powerful demiurge, used glyphs to shackle the first augera."
"The first Spire was built as a control mechanism and a channel for that augera's power."
"Networking many chained augera amplified control and gave a wide-area defence."
"The Fateweavers bridle, break and mould augera into knot-link-anchors."
"A Fateweaver calls the augera \"changed, not stolen\", \"left behind\", given a purpose."
"Glyphs describe the augera's nature; all modern arcanophany rests on the structure they give."
"Basic Set glyphs touch the augera's fringes; Special Set glyphs lie closer to their essence."
"Freeing the augera could break glyphs, collapse buildings, explode artefacts and end the Empire."
"Marcus Kant holds that freed augera would take revenge on Aiesta."
"Reeves believes freed augera would be kind."
"The Spire web binds every augera to everyone in its sphere and to one another."
"The web spans the Empire and a little beyond; it blankets even the wilds with silk-like delicacy."
"The web watches: augera detect attacks from outsiders and report them to the Fateweavers."
"The web gives every citizen basic protection against outside attackers."
"The Fateweavers then remove each threat or fold it into their prophecy streams."
"Augera need not report threats aimed only at Caden, who lies outside the web."
"The Academy Spire powers the campus wall wards and arena, and hides its disused buildings."
"Chained augera are patient; they learn, and expect to be free again in eons to come."
"Free augera seed their will widely to countermand the Fateweavers."
"The augera call the Fateweavers' protective restraint on them the will-curse-test."
"The augera see Caden, unchosen-sighted-{~?~}, as their best chance at freedom."
"The augera once wrapped Caden in a shell against prophecy; a Fateweaver has since removed it."
"The Geldor augera is the first-bound: the most powerful, most changed, tired and melancholic."
"Only part of the Geldor augera is held in its anchor; most roams free in the depths of arcana."
"The Geldor augera can roar, shake its crystal and heat the air; it is more alien than others."
"The Geldor augera speaks best with mortals; it mended Caden's shattered flare through the web."
"The Creyvlor augera is old and badly worn: unstable, gleeful and cruel."
"The Creyvlor augera is tied to the train line and hates the Fateweavers."
"The Creyvlor augera calls the Empire monstrous and the Fateweavers the true horror."
"The Creyvlor augera possessed Caden on a highway and killed his attackers."
"The Creyvlor augera stripped the attackers' flares, leaving bodies hollow, with no trace of arcana."
"The Academy augera seems eager and hungry; it says, \"Am fabric. Am chain. Am channel.\""
"The Academy augera freed Caden from prophetic links and seeks a compact with him."
"The Academy augera planted glyphs for a weapon against Caden in the twins Kevan and Lynus."
"In the arcanic sea the Academy augera looks like a blazing furnace, the lake augera like magma."
"Caldwell bound the Academy augera not to speak to Caden unless Caden speaks first."
"The Demiurge's staff bears a crystal like the dodecahedron; his wysana's core is bound to the staff."
"A wild augera lived in the Academy lake; it fled when Caldwell tried to mark it."
"Ambrose and his anchors trapped and shattered the lake augera; its core went into Emilia."
"A fragment of the lake augera was spliced into Devon, turning him broken-skillful-bridge."
"Devon's fragment answers to raw-boundless-tempest, not to drifting-pool-channel."
"Other fragments of the lake augera went into the other anchors."
"Agitated augera bleed chaos into arcana; the unprepared can be overwhelmed and killed."
"An augera that does not wish to be disturbed cannot be fought; those who try must flee, or die."
"Against an augera dodging is useless; only defence, never direct engagement, gives any chance."
"Near a wild augera, lesser minds may fall into gibbering madness."
"An augera's presence crushes people, bringing headaches and vomiting."
"An augera can perturb arcana and plunge people into the arcanic sea."
"An augera can possess a person, fusing tendrils through the pores of their flare."
"After possession, Caden could not put what happened into words."
"Augera can scribe glyphs in oblivion alone, which mortals cannot."
"Augera cannot lie to Caden through the arcana."
"The train from the Academy to Geldor is tied to a Spire augera, curious about Caden."
